[Style] Both call sites pass a `String`, and the catch variable is unused.

```suggestion
  private static long parseLong(@Nullable String value) {
    if (value == null) {
      return 0;
    }
    try {
      return new BigInteger(value).longValueExact();
    } catch (NumberFormatException ignored) {
      return 0;
    }
  }
```

[General] Separately, returning `0` for a malformed value emits a false sample (e.g. `completed=100, total=0`). Skipping the entry, as the overflow path does, would be safer.

