[Style] `AttributesBuilder.put(String, String)` funnels into `AttributeKey.stringKey(key)`, which builds a fresh key object on every call — and `buildAttributes` runs once per in-flight compaction on every collection cycle. Holding the keys as constants is the usual pattern here and avoids that churn:

```java
  private static final AttributeKey<String> TASK_TYPE =
      AttributeKey.stringKey("cassandra.compaction.task_type");
  private static final AttributeKey<String> KEYSPACE = AttributeKey.stringKey("cassandra.keyspace");
  private static final AttributeKey<String> TABLE = AttributeKey.stringKey("cassandra.table");
```

`buildAttributes` then collapses to:

```java
  private static Attributes buildAttributes(String taskType, String keyspace, String columnFamily) {
    return Attributes.of(TASK_TYPE, taskType, KEYSPACE, keyspace, TABLE, columnFamily);
  }
```

Not a `suggestion` block since it spans both spots — needs `import io.opentelemetry.api.common.AttributeKey;` and drops the now-unused `AttributesBuilder` import.

